---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="ASME B36.10-2022 — Welded & Seamless Wrought Steel Pipe | HowNote"
  description="HowNote reference page for ASME B36.10-2022 with official scope, evidence labels and linked pipe tools."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <div class="eyebrow">HowSpec · Standard Lookup</div>
    <h1>ASME B36.10-2022</h1>
    <p>Welded and Seamless Wrought Steel Pipe</p>
    <div class="badge-row">
      <span class="badge badge-official">OFFICIAL metadata</span>
      <span class="badge">2022 edition</span>
      <span class="badge">Pipe / Tube</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container standard-layout related-section">
    <article class="panel prose-card">
      <h2>Official scope summary</h2>
      <p>ASME describes B36.10 as covering the standardization of dimensions of welded and seamless wrought steel pipe for high or low temperatures and pressures.</p>
      <p>The official ASME product page currently identifies the 2022 edition and states that the standard is on stabilized maintenance.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://www.asme.org/codes-standards/find-codes-standards/welded-and-seamless-wrought-steel-pipe" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the official ASME page →</a>

      <h2>What HowNote publishes</h2>
      <p>HowNote currently publishes official identity and edition metadata, plus a deliberately small Schedule 40 reference subset whose OD, wall thickness and nominal mass have been cross-checked against manufacturer publications.</p>
      <p>HowNote does not reproduce the complete paid ASME dimension table and does not present a manufacturer chart as the official standard text.</p>

      <h2>How to use this page</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the nominal-size converter to match DN, NPS and regional A labels.</li>
        <li>Use the pipe calculator to calculate theoretical mass from actual geometry and density.</li>
        <li>Review the original standard before issuing an engineering specification or purchase order.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <aside class="panel standard-facts">
      <div class="eyebrow">Standard facts</div>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Designation</dt><dd>ASME B36.10</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Edition</dt><dd>2022</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Title</dt><dd>Welded and Seamless Wrought Steel Pipe</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Organization</dt><dd>ASME</dd></div>
        <div><dt>HowNote evidence</dt><dd>Official metadata + manufacturer cross-check + calculated values</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Last HowNote verification</dt><dd>August 21, 2026</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button" href="/tools/pipe-weight-calculator">Pipe calculator</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/sizes">Size reference</a>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
